#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068844 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068451 :question/id #uuid "d53c6172-978d-57c7-b1f0-e56e892e48a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10997" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06161b70-c2b1-55cf-b1de-7e7405481b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272443} {:answer/id #uuid "39421cbc-ac97-518d-bd42-917038547d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272887} {:answer/id #uuid "444dd661-b7e1-574e-8d5f-f13ae9f6b31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y}=2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272968} {:answer/id #uuid "56d2005e-9587-5d20-848f-63f6e43bb679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2y}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273128} {:answer/id #uuid "b3af1ba1-131e-5620-89ed-6381153a413f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{y}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06161b70-c2b1-55cf-b1de-7e7405481b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272443} :answer-field/id #uuid "45330bec-555f-5499-99ad-e898e9a6b68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274751}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8653163f-c134-5fe5-8ca8-a073f08d08b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154359" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6d452c-ba79-5770-b07f-d5b3da22c242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273029} {:answer/id #uuid "65ede7b4-590b-55e3-8f50-17be1122ce29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273261} {:answer/id #uuid "787ea476-0dcb-5e79-83e8-2015f52616e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273413} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd47fee-b75d-5148-b300-321c7b06ff4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274013} {:answer/id #uuid "bd385d42-fd70-5ecd-bff1-d953008c20fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65ede7b4-590b-55e3-8f50-17be1122ce29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273261} :answer-field/id #uuid "66f205c9-d7de-5191-ae98-7d9196548f1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274811}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc5a6535-55d7-58bf-9da3-473b544214d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154367" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\,$ for $\\,|y|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae3c5e0-1352-56fd-ba70-9a98aacdb051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250782} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8d8918-9739-590c-9fbc-5d363870224a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251048} {:answer/id #uuid "7590b4e3-175b-5973-b9a4-23a24a9d8b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251521} {:answer/id #uuid "d65bc188-62c5-5f03-8494-a8fcd839865a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252450} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc7213-5543-5c22-a097-9b55ce7076ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc7213-5543-5c22-a097-9b55ce7076ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252486} :answer-field/id #uuid "d173063d-47e4-520d-a7a8-338e552ab61b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253168}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a130453a-6065-5959-8de8-bb802e7d41f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-118885" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272345 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b4d2f7-6de2-5196-b879-a739a65217f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269464} {:answer/id #uuid "6d70ab15-788c-5c79-a3c0-32dd56d91377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270240} {:answer/id #uuid "9562133f-63b5-500a-8c0d-b36151b151b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270580} {:answer/id #uuid "d007c7f5-5f1d-5941-b941-1b46c8f9d226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271095} {:answer/id #uuid "e3317b49-f544-53b2-a03e-5508bdec7af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d70ab15-788c-5c79-a3c0-32dd56d91377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270240} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0697db-7cb2-5930-925b-39436791038a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271900}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8ed818f-2b3f-54cd-b6b2-99b0955850e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-14246" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{x}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a0c82e4-a410-5545-aba6-e6bc3809dd5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272760} {:answer/id #uuid "632f8488-1426-51de-b79c-859a00953830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273240} {:answer/id #uuid "8f09bfeb-fa40-5b8c-a65a-f33bf93f0996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273624} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa6a988-751b-5fc3-92dd-5e4dfbf0e530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273767} {:answer/id #uuid "df59ea5f-fed1-5499-abd7-c6c018da530f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df59ea5f-fed1-5499-abd7-c6c018da530f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274358} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a01516-b9bc-55d0-ac76-1962bc75b5ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275011}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2654f6e-f38e-5fe7-bd83-e2905edb3c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-154357" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcb38c3-d1e9-539a-b4e1-dab540d43230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272494} {:answer/id #uuid "658178ae-c54b-516e-b636-4665fc326043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273257} {:answer/id #uuid "74e2bd65-0d26-5b57-8915-d0995c4f7d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273386} {:answer/id #uuid "ab807a16-6387-5feb-ab59-267a4f6a3481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273867} {:answer/id #uuid "facac07e-06f2-51b9-b250-6d1ff2d92eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e2bd65-0d26-5b57-8915-d0995c4f7d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273386} :answer-field/id #uuid "465b078e-0db8-5efa-8088-98d975791b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274753}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c3a88f3-b655-5d1c-832a-8fe5b3af13b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-154361" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e68c45d-09d4-569c-b913-79d7d46d8f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272658} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1adc60-82c0-5aa8-884b-65f615105a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272780} {:answer/id #uuid "42810437-8763-58f8-a94c-d08f4ca51719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272958} {:answer/id #uuid "88432955-bb9d-5cdb-8168-f7b9543320c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273557} {:answer/id #uuid "a15158a7-e04f-5b2b-9783-52add73727d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1adc60-82c0-5aa8-884b-65f615105a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272780} :answer-field/id #uuid "09996012-870f-5883-938b-a22328b3e885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274650}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e20f2fcf-b4a2-51d2-acda-66700b834327" :question/math-academy-id "q-154369" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{-y}(x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{e}^{-y}(x-1) \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb8f22b-8ca5-57ef-8370-d2d3c166b579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272810} {:answer/id #uuid "37747715-a217-5cdf-adc1-7537938bdbc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272874} {:answer/id #uuid "bf41e0ba-cb23-53f6-b183-adf43eec5717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274039} {:answer/id #uuid "d2409366-319f-54f1-9e94-19f43f971322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274225} {:answer/id #uuid "fadaeede-fe79-5093-a9c2-59e6513e62b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf41e0ba-cb23-53f6-b183-adf43eec5717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274039} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06779cf-201b-5aa3-8047-f9fa3b7c1ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274942}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b80541f-68bf-590f-9d99-5d43ea712334" :question/math-academy-id "q-154373" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7988d84c-0ea4-5988-8ba2-c95a358645a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273430} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b829dd-2a25-59c2-94a0-d8a65efff454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273853} {:answer/id #uuid "c09a28a4-9df6-5a65-b137-e6409c6a24dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274058} {:answer/id #uuid "c397d6c5-1419-560a-b38e-5dbaf38f637e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274085} {:answer/id #uuid "efb5eff8-9bff-5df3-93d8-810704b8cbff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7988d84c-0ea4-5988-8ba2-c95a358645a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273430} :answer-field/id #uuid "21509f54-1783-5348-95f3-0c5cd428b6f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274696}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "448a7a77-8f84-5ac7-87e1-3803e2799bbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-158035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c8a0d36-f6e2-5a0a-89e6-2d26ad013533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272639} {:answer/id #uuid "64177146-09d3-586f-a38e-d67e4b445b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273246} {:answer/id #uuid "69ce8b4d-9357-5dca-8786-946b6bd0da61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273300} {:answer/id #uuid "8242ae78-fb2f-5486-ada7-1e349d52072c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273503} {:answer/id #uuid "c1de0088-404a-5b93-9e68-eab2a6e24abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡y=\\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64177146-09d3-586f-a38e-d67e4b445b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273246} :answer-field/id #uuid "96425cca-34f0-5837-934b-74d6042e90fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274895}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0b5140d-8021-52c8-9880-109bb8e78b6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158116" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y}$ for $x\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d153f63-b757-54a0-920b-62e754969c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272788} {:answer/id #uuid "56b00252-91b0-5b60-8e8f-804dca0617c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273126} {:answer/id #uuid "d4879ac6-9572-5560-9ee7-27001a2d76ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274251} {:answer/id #uuid "e9eae476-aba3-55b4-b017-91ac6b9a54ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274458} {:answer/id #uuid "fd235e72-e654-5d2c-b2d3-bbc9bacb1db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd235e72-e654-5d2c-b2d3-bbc9bacb1db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274610} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a4727f-caa7-5dcd-91c3-adb929275f98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c9d63db-85c4-5f46-a91d-0a91ded8b499" :question/math-academy-id "q-158117" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068873 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068672 :question/id #uuid "2acac780-2b17-5489-accc-2a3a090784e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-9927" :question/problem "Rewrite the expression $(x^2 + 14x + 49) - 8$ as the difference between a perfect square and a constant." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\nx^2 + {\\color{red}{2}}{\\color{blue}{a}}x + a^2 = (x + {\\color{blue}{a}})^2\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+14x+49 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+14x+{7}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 7x+{7}^{2} & = \\\\ (x+7{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+14x+49)-8 & = \\\\ (x+7{)}^{2}-8 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f10e4a34-a512-5ff4-abbc-66e6830d63d0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bba58eb-ca45-57fa-b7eb-7a8cd5800a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 3)^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065728} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe0877d-2022-51a3-b14b-88470a8de575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 3)^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065729} {:answer/id #uuid "01d858ec-3a76-591a